{
  "root_cause": "The datepicker component prevents the default Tab key behavior when the popup is open, blocking focus movement to the next form field. This occurs because the Vanilla Calendar Pro (VCP) library, integrated via the datepicker component, traps focus within the popup and prevents tabbing out.",
  "repair_strategy": "Add a keydown listener for the Tab key on the input element when the datepicker popup is shown. This listener hides the popup, allowing the Tab key to proceed with its default focus-changing behavior. The listener is removed when the popup is hidden or the component is disposed to avoid memory leaks.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "js/src/datepicker.ts",
      "sha256": "333ada052b9200667edf9078b105036dee5c1406a86e3865f6534e2ddb18c53a",
      "before": "  protected declare _onTriggerClick: () => void

  constructor(element?: string | Element | null, config?: Partial<DatepickerConfig> | null) {
",
      "after": "  protected declare _onTriggerClick: () => void
  protected declare _onTabKeyDown: ((event: KeyboardEvent) => void) | null;

  constructor(element?: string | Element | null, config?: Partial<DatepickerConfig> | null) {
"
    },
    {
      "path": "js/src/datepicker.ts",
      "sha256": "333ada052b9200667edf9078b105036dee5c1406a86e3865f6534e2ddb18c53a",
      "before": "    this._calendar.show()
    this._isShown = true

    EventHandler.trigger(this._element, EVENT_SHOWN)
  }
",
      "after": "    this._calendar.show()
    this._isShown = true

    EventHandler.trigger(this._element, EVENT_SHOWN)

    // ADD: Add tab key listener to hide popup on Tab key
    if (this._isInput) {
      this._onTabKeyDown = (event: KeyboardEvent) => {
        if (event.key === 'Tab') {
          this.hide();
        }
      };
      this._element.addEventListener('keydown', this._onTabKeyDown);
    }
  }
"
    },
    {
      "path": "js/src/datepicker.ts",
      "sha256": "333ada052b9200667edf9078b105036dee5c1406a86e3865f6534e2ddb18c53a",
      "before": "    this._calendar.hide()
    this._isShown = false

    EventHandler.trigger(this._element, EVENT_HIDDEN)
  }
",
      "after": "    this._calendar.hide()
    this._isShown = false

    EventHandler.trigger(this._element, EVENT_HIDDEN)

    // REMOVE: Remove tab key listener
    if (this._isInput && this._onTabKeyDown) {
      this._element.removeEventListener('keydown', this._onTabKeyDown);
      this._onTabKeyDown = null;
    }
  }
"
    },
    {
      "path": "js/src/datepicker.ts",
      "sha256": "333ada052b9200667edf9078b105036dee5c1406a86e3865f6534e2ddb18c53a",
      "before": "    this._calendar = null
    super.dispose()
  }
",
      "after": "    this._calendar = null

    // REMOVE: Remove tab key listener if not already removed
    if (this._isInput && this._onTabKeyDown) {
      this._element.removeEventListener('keydown', this._onTabKeyDown);
      this._onTabKeyDown = null;
    }

    super.dispose()
  }
"
    }
  ],
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "Tab key navigation will move focus from the departure date field to the passengers field when the datepicker popup is open, restoring expected form tab order behavior.",
  "functional_risks": [
    "Hiding the popup on Tab key press may interrupt date selection if the user intends to tab through the calendar grid (though the calendar grid is not focusable in this implementation).",
    "Rapid successive Tab presses may cause multiple hide/show cycles, though the _isShown flag prevents redundant operations.",
    "The fix assumes the Tab key is the only key requiring unblocked navigation; Shift+Tab is not addressed but follows the same pattern.",
    "If VCP internally relies on preventing Tab for its own focus management, this change could cause unexpected focus behavior within the calendar (though the calendar is not focusable in input mode)."
  ],
  "verification_requirements": [
    "Verify that pressing Tab from the departure date field moves focus to the passengers field when the datepicker popup is open.",
    "Verify that pressing Tab from the departure date field moves focus to the passengers field when the datepicker popup is closed (no regression).",
    "Verify that pressing Escape still closes the datepicker popup (regression guard).",
    "Verify that date selection via mouse or keyboard within the popup still functions correctly.",
    "Verify that the popup hides when tabbing out and does not remain open."
  ]
}
